; Desktop Subsystem for Android (DSA)
; The user's add-on disk (dsa-addons.rc). When the host attaches one, init mounts its partition
; (/dev/block/by-name/dsa_addons, an erofs file system) read only at /mnt/dsa-addons, its files
; labelled as system files, before /data. dsa-gapps.rc and dsa-arm-translation.rc then mount
; the add-on images in it straight from their files: erofs opens each file with init's
; credentials as init mounts it, and reads it with them afterwards. init already reads and
; searches system files, so the files need no rule of their own.
(allow init tmpfs (dir (mounton)))

; The disk's superblock. Nothing is laid over or bound from the disk itself, only from the
; images mounted from its files, which have superblocks of their own (gapps.cil,
; arm-translation.cil); a statfs of /mnt/dsa-addons is checked against this type. As an
; fs_type it is covered by the platform's "allow domain fs_type:filesystem getattr". It is a
; contextmount_type because the platform forbids relabelling a superblock to any other
; fs_type; the platform keeps such types read-only, and nothing writes to the disk.
(type dsa_addons_fs)
(roletype object_r dsa_addons_fs)
(typeattributeset fs_type (dsa_addons_fs))
(typeattributeset contextmount_type (dsa_addons_fs))
; init mounts the disk with fscontext=dsa_addons_fs and context=system_file. The kernel
; relabels the superblock from erofs's own type (relabelfrom labeledfs, relabelto the disk's
; type); labels every file system_file, the root first (relabelfrom the disk's type, and
; system_file associates with it); and then checks the mount against the disk's type.
; system_file is a file type, not an fs_type, so the platform's neverallow on an fs_type
; associating with a file type does not reach it.
(allow init labeledfs (filesystem (relabelfrom)))
(allow init dsa_addons_fs (filesystem (mount relabelfrom relabelto)))
(allow system_file dsa_addons_fs (filesystem (associate)))
